@startuml "State - Order (Solution) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title An order that forwards to its state

class Order <<Context>> {
  - state : OrderState
  + pay()
  + ship(trackingNumber)
  + failDelivery()
  + deliver()
  + cancel()
}
interface OrderState <<State, sealed>> {
  + pay(Order) : OrderState
  + ship(Order, trackingNumber) : OrderState
  + failDelivery(Order) : OrderState
  + deliver(Order) : OrderState
  + cancel(Order) : OrderState
}
class Placed <<record>>
class Paid <<record>>
class Shipped <<record>> {
  trackingNumber : String
  failedAttempts : int
}
class Delivered <<record>>
class Cancelled <<record>>

Order o--> OrderState
OrderState <|.. Placed
OrderState <|.. Paid
OrderState <|.. Shipped
OrderState <|.. Delivered
OrderState <|.. Cancelled

note right of OrderState
  <b>Each operation returns the next state.</b>
  By default every operation is refused;
  a state overrides only what it allows.
end note
note bottom of Shipped
  <b>Its data belongs to this shipment.</b>
  A new shipment starts at zero attempts.
end note
@enduml
